eeded if you don't want to go through a whole involved process of getting a specialist to cast an oneiroscope, convincing a dream-hunting creature to show you the way, or burning through Glamour to force the creation of multiple gates that form nightmares in their wake, after which point you still can't use dreamscaping, suffer a penalty to other oneiromancy and oneiromachy, and can't simply wake up to immediately leave the dream. For most practical purposes you're better off trying to get the target to consent to your visit beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}